cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ThoughtDAG in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "ThoughtDAG: an instrument for legible human-AI collaboration"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Chen"
    given-names: "Xia"
repository-code: "https://github.com/chenxiachan/thoughtdag"
url: "https://github.com/chenxiachan/thoughtdag"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - human-AI interaction
  - context engineering
  - reasoning graph
  - research instrument
  - large language models
abstract: >-
  ThoughtDAG turns LLM conversations into an editable thought graph on an
  infinite canvas. One rule governs everything: a wire is context. The
  instrument keeps human-AI collaboration legible: context assembly is
  visible and layered, every generation records an upstream fingerprint,
  stale answers are flagged and replayable in dependency order, and runs
  export as auditable manifests. Reusable workflow templates (paradigms)
  let researchers design, run, and re-run reasoning experiments.
